###  http://data.europa.eu/949/railInclination
:railInclination rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf :trackObjParameter ,
                                    :vehicleTypeTechnicalObjectCharacteristic ;
                 rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                 rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                             :RunningTrack
                                             :VehicleType
                                           )
                             ] ;
                 rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                 :XMLName "ITP_RailInclination" ;
                 :applicable "Y" ;
                 :eratvIndex "4.6.5" ;
                 :formatNote "In XML the accepted value is NN, where N is a digit from 0 to 9."@en ;
                 :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/rail-inclinations/RailInclinations> ;
                 :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                 :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.4.3" ;
                 :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/RailInclination> ,
                                           <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/RailInclinationSKOS> ;
                 :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2022-10-20"^^xsd:date ,
                                                     "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ,
                                                     "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1299/2023-09-28> ;
                 rdfs:comment "An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail relative to the running surface."@en ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                 rdfs:label "Rail inclination"@en ;
                 rdfs:seeAlso "INF TSI:4.2.4.7" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """This inclination is in most cases expressed for MS globally, but anyway it requires presentation for the specific track, when in one SoL more values occur.
An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail when installed in the track relative to the plane of the rails (running surface), equal to the angle between the axis of symmetry of the rail (or of an equivalent symmetrical rail having the same rail head profile) and the perpendicular to the plane of the rails. The typical values for the railway inclination are 1:20, 1:30, 1:40."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/reasonsEtcsRadioBlockCenterReject
:reasonsEtcsRadioBlockCenterReject rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf :tsiCompliantTrainProtectionSystemObjParameter ;
                                   rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain :RadioBlockCenter ;
                                   rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                                   :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
                                   :dependencyNote "A value has to be provided when ETCS is present (a value is provided on 1.1.1.3.2.1)."@en ;
                                   :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/etcs-rbc-reject-reasons/ETCSRBCRejectionReasons> ;
                                   :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                                   :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.2.15" ,
                                              "1.2.1.1.1.15" ;
                                   :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ReasonsEtcsRadioBlockCenterReject> ,
                                                             <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ReasonsEtcsRadioBlockCenterRejectSKOS> ;
                                   :tsiOPEAppendixD3Index "1.4" ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-11-07"^^xsd:date ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                       "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                       "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :etcsLevelType ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
                                   rdfs:comment "List of cases subject to system design choices made by the infrastructure manager according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"@en ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Reasons for which an ETCS Radio Block Center can reject a train"@en ;
                                   rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/domains/technical-specifications-interoperability/control-command-and-signalling-tsi_en#oe-content-paragraph-1632"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """1. Distinguish between mandatory and optional: decision was only to record the mandatory ones, but optional reasons can be added.
2. Providing the non-implemented CR-solution which have been accepted by IM, after check/approval with RU's, is also allowed."""@en .


